# .gitattributes — per-path git behaviour overrides.
#
# Phase 260516-kya / Plan 01 — secret-leak hard gate, defense-in-depth.
#
# `-diff` suppresses content rendering in `git diff`, `git log -p`, and
# the GitHub PR diff UI. Even if a `.env` file is accidentally staged,
# the leaked content will not be displayed to a reviewer. This is a
# belt-and-braces complement to lefthook + CI gitleaks gates: even when
# the gate would block the COMMIT, the diff-suppression prevents the
# secret from surfacing in render previews of staged-but-unfinalised
# changes (e.g. IDE diff panes).
.env*    -diff
.env.bak -diff
